#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:1
msgid "`vtkFidesReader` supports reading from `Conduit` nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:3
msgid ""
"The `vtkFidesReader`, which historically only supported reading from ADIOS2 "
"files, now allows you to pass in-memory Conduit nodes directly into the "
"`vtkFidesReader`, bypassing the filesystem entirely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:5
msgid ""
"**Expected Usage** You can provide data sources via both C++ and Python. The "
"reader relies on a JSON data model where the data source type is explicitly "
"given as `\"conduit\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:8
msgid "In C++ (using the Conduit C-API):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:10
msgid ""
"conduit_node* c_node = conduit::c_node(&my_cpp_node);\n"
"reader->SetDataSourceNode(\"source\", c_node);\n"
"reader->Update();\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:16
msgid "In Python:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:18
msgid ""
"# node is a standard conduit.Node populated with numpy arrays\n"
"reader.SetDataSourceNode(\"source\", node)\n"
"reader.Update()\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:24
msgid ""
"To clear a previously set resource, you can pass `nullptr` (or `None` in "
"Python). Note that doing so will leave the reader in an invalid state until "
"a new, valid data source is provided for the pipeline to update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:26
msgid "**Known Issues and Caveats**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:27
msgid ""
"**Memory Ownership (C++):** The reader **does not** take ownership of the "
"memory backing the `conduit_node`. You are strictly responsible for ensuring "
"the data backing the node remains valid and unmodified until the VTK "
"pipeline execution (`Update()`) has completely finished."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:28
msgid ""
"**Memory Ownership (Python):** The reader will automatically increment the "
"reference count of the provided Python `conduit.Node`, preventing standard "
"garbage collection. However, if your Conduit node is just a view into "
"externally managed memory (like a C++ simulation array or a volatile NumPy "
"view), you must ensure that external memory is not freed while the reader "
"holds the reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:29
msgid ""
"**Partition Indexing:** Because Conduit nodes represent local in-memory "
"snapshots, the resulting `vtkPartitionedDataSet` uses local index geometries "
"(starting at `0`) rather than ADIOS2's globally offset indices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/iofides-supports-conduit.md:30
msgid ""
"**Build Requirements:** While still present in the api, the Python overload "
"of `SetDataSourceNode` is disabled if VTK is compiled without Python "
"wrapping (`VTK_WRAP_PYTHON=OFF`) or if the underlying Conduit library was "
"built without Python support. Similarly, the C++ overload of "
"`SetDataSourceNode` is disabled if VTK is compiled without Conduit support."
msgstr ""
